ref 17592186045417] [17592186250976 #edb/ref 1080 "{6}^{x}ln⁡6-10{x}^{2}+6x" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186250976 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186250976 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "3232bdcf-d781-5e59-bb5b-56c10f0d7fa1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186251009 #edb/ref 1080 "{6}^{x}-10{x}^{2}+6x-19" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186251009 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186251009 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "37865371-b061-54aa-9810-81e59d0b835b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186251060 #edb/ref 1080 "{6}^{x}ln⁡6-10x+6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186251060 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186251060 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "3d09661f-ce26-5e19-a8b8-2ae50263662e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186251775 #edb/ref 1080 "{6}^{x}-10x+6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186251775 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186251775 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "9007950f-ce55-5f0c-a1f6-d3963f0294f9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186252214 #edb/ref 1080 "{6}^{x}ln⁡6-10{x}^{2}+6x-19" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186252214 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186252214 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "bbf32e0c-8341-5060-b67e-c44870ab4cd0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186253210 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186250976 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186253210 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186251009 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186253210 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186251060 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186253210 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186251775 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186253210 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186252214 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186253210 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186253210 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186253210 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186251060 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186253210 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "e849ca6e-9bda-5244-a669-0f22826facaa" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186253334 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186253210 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186253334 #edb/ref 1069 "q-11735" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186253334 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186253334 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that $f(x)={6}^{x}-5{x}^{2}+6x-19$, find ${f}^{′}(x).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186253334 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "50678a5c-afcb-522f-98fb-80e9680afca6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186253334 #edb/ref 1074 "Applying the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({6}^{x}-5{x}^{2}+6x-19) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({6}^{x})-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(5{x}^{2})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(6x)-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(19) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({6}^{x})-5\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2})+6\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x)-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(19) \\\\  & =ln⁡6\\cdot {6}^{x}-5(2x)+6(1)-0 \\\\  & ={6}^{x}ln⁡6-10x+6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186408166 #edb/ref 10 :answer-field.type/checkbox #edb/ref 17592186045416] [17592186409262 #edb/ref 1146 #edb/ref 17592186251060 #edb/ref 17592186045416] [17592186409262 #edb/ref 1148 101.998 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186409262 #edb/ref 1156 #edb/ref 17592186409263 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186409262 #edb/ref 1158 #edb/ref 17592186253334 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186409262 #edb/ref 1161 #uuid "2400d6f0-de9d-4711-a743-56063c38ea56" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186409262 #edb/ref 1162 #edb/ref 17592186045571 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186420504 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186477605 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186420504 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186477606 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186420504 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186477607 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186420504 #edb/ref 1069 "q-37456" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420504 #edb/ref 1071 "The function \n$f(x,y)$ \nhas the second derivative\n\n$$\n\\boldsymbol{f}^{″}(x,y)=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nand has a stationary point at $(1,1).$ If $H$ denotes the Hessian determinant of $f,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $H(1,1)>0$\n\nII. $\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}}(1,1)>0$\n\nIII. The point $(1,1)$ is a local minimum of $f$\n\nSelect all that apply." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186420504 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d1a7556c-36af-5f0b-b64c-a00089e6850e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420504 #edb/ref 1074 "The second partial derivative test states that if $a\\in {R}^{2}$ is a stationary point of $f(x,y)$ with Hessian determinant $H(a),$ we have the following:\n\n- If $H(a)>0,$ then:\n\n- if $\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}}(a)<0,$ then $f$ has a local maximum at $a$\n\n- if $\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}}(a)>0,$ then $f$ has a local minimum at $a$\n\n- If $H(a)<0,$ then $f$ has a saddle point at $a$\n\n- If $H(a)=0,$ then the second partial derivatives test is inconclusive.\n\nEvaluating the second derivative at $(1,1),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(1,1)=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Indeed, computing the determinant of ${f}^{″}(1,1),$ we get\n\n$$\nH(1,1)=det({f}^{″}(1,1))=2\\cdot 0-{1}^{2}=-1<0.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, we have $\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}}(1,1)=({f}^{″}(1,1))_{11}=2>0.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $H(1,1)<0,$ then $(1,1)$ is a saddle point by the second partial derivative test.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186477271 #edb/ref 1080 "false" #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186477271 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186477271 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "f54eb3dc-8f1a-5dd1-962f-c6bca73b03cb" #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186477272 #edb/ref 1080 "true" #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186477272 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [